  "verbalization": "Isoliquiritigenin is implicated in the regulation of the Epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) through a multi-step mechanism involving the interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, each linking Isoliquiritigenin to the EGFR via different intermediates. The first two paths directly connect Isoliquiritigenin to the EGFR through the interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha, while the third path provides a more complex, albeit still valid, route through a long-chain metabolite that ultimately targets the EGFR. The scores from these paths suggest a consistent and plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism of the third path remains less clear. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforces the likelihood of a functional connection between Isoliquiritigenin and EGFR, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular interactions involved.",
